@startuml SequenceTakeAndGrade
' Scenario 2 — A student sits an exam and a teacher grades it
' The longest flow in the system; covers the timer, autosave and the publish gate.

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

actor Student
actor Teacher
participant "TakeExamPage" as Take
participant "SubmissionDetailPage" as Detail
box "Server" #F8FAFC
  participant "SubmissionService" as Svc
  participant "grading.js" as Grade
  participant "SubmissionRepository" as Repo
end box
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Opening the exam ==

Student -> Take : opens the exam
Take -> Svc : POST /api/exams/:id/attempt
Svc -> Repo : createAttempt(examId, studentId, expiresAt)
Repo -> DB : INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING *
note right of Repo
  Idempotent: two simultaneous requests
  (a double click, React's dev double
  effect) cannot create two attempts.
  expires_at is fixed NOW, so a later
  change to the exam duration cannot move
  a deadline already running.
end note
DB --> Repo : the attempt row
Repo --> Svc : Submission
Svc --> Take : { submission, secondsRemaining }
Take -> Student : renders questions + countdown

== Answering (repeats) ==

Student -> Take : types an answer
Take -> Take : debounce 1.2s
Take -> Svc : PATCH /api/attempts/:id/draft
Svc -> Svc : reject if expired or already submitted
Svc -> Repo : saveDraft(answers)
Repo -> DB : INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (submission_id, question_id)\nDO UPDATE
note right of DB
  Answers live in the database, not the
  browser. Closing the tab loses nothing.
end note

== Submitting ==

alt the student clicks Submit
  Student -> Take : clicks Submit
  Take -> Svc : POST /api/attempts/:id/submit { auto: false }
  Svc -> Svc : refuse if past expires_at
else the countdown reaches zero
  Take -> Svc : POST /api/attempts/:id/submit { auto: true }
  Svc -> Svc : deadline waived — the answers were\ncaptured before expiry
end

Svc -> Grade : scoreMultipleChoice(question, value)
note right of Grade
  Multiple choice is marked here, from the
  answer key. Deterministic, no model, and
  it cannot be inconsistent between runs.
end note
Svc -> Repo : submit(scored)
Repo -> DB : UPDATE submissions SET status='submitted'
note right of Svc
  The overall grade is NOT computed. The
  submission stays ungraded until a teacher
  acts on it.
end note
Svc --> Take : submission
Take -> Student : redirect to Grades — no grade shown yet

== Grading ==

Teacher -> Detail : opens the submission
Detail -> Svc : GET /api/submissions/:id
Svc -> Svc : verify this teacher OWNS the exam
Svc --> Detail : submission + exam WITH the answer key

Teacher -> Detail : scores the open-text answers
Detail -> Detail : preview total live, same formula as the server
Teacher -> Detail : clicks Save draft
Detail -> Svc : PATCH /api/submissions/:id/grade { publish: false }

Svc -> Grade : computeGrade(questions, scores)
note right of Grade
  grade = sum(score x weight) / sum(weight)
  Multiple-choice scores sent by the client
  are ignored; the answer key decides.
end note
Svc -> Repo : saveGrades(status='ai_graded')
Repo -> DB : UPDATE ... graded_at stays NULL

Student -> Detail : (checks their grades)
note over Student
  Still sees nothing. The status is even
  collapsed to 'submitted', so the student
  cannot tell a draft grade exists.
end note

== Publishing ==

Teacher -> Detail : clicks Publish grade
Detail -> Svc : POST /api/submissions/:id/publish
Svc -> Repo : saveGrades(status='graded', graded_at=now())
Repo -> DB : UPDATE submissions
note right of DB
  A CHECK constraint enforces that 'graded'
  implies both a grade and a graded_at, so
  no code path can leave a submission
  half-published.
end note
Svc --> Detail : submission
Student -> Student : the grade and feedback are now visible

@enduml
